# Target C: independent exact audit of the nine-no-root k=6 p=4 m=5 closure

Date: 2026-10-04
Base main: `883a88ea86b9dfaf9d7843aa18ce0d8b6324c49d`
Status: exact finite re-verification of the m=5 slice. C-II and Level I remain open.

This audit concerns the nine-no-root branch

```text
k=6, D=-2, d_root=1, p=4, m=5.
```

The established structural reductions force rank `P=3` on nine external
coordinates, generalized weights at least `(3,4,6)`, exactly four touched
singleton root blocks, singleton touch multiplicity at least four,
touched-complete root nullity at most one, and external relation-rank increment
exactly six.

The earlier corrected m=5 note recorded an exact census, but its executed
verifier source was not committed. I independently reconstructed the exact K8
quotient-coordinate calculation and reran the full finite enumeration.

## Enumeration

All five-support families were enumerated and quotiented by the full `S_7`
action. There are exactly 137 five-support family orbits. For each family, the
support multiplicity assignment was quotiented by the support stabilizer. Each
admissible four-singleton root choice was then quotiented by the
multiplicity-preserving stabilizer. Every remaining no-root cycle orientation
and every one of the `3^4` singleton local-direction assignments was tested.

The three possible support multiplicity profiles give:

```text
profile          root orbits  oriented  local-dir  rank(P)=3  weight-pass
(3,3,1,1,1)             78       2106     170586       4775          144
(3,2,2,1,1)             47       3807     308367       3872          356
(2,2,2,2,1)             10       2430     196830       2284          324
```

The generalized-weight profiles of the surviving rank-three coefficient
spaces are:

```text
(3,3,1,1,1):
  (3,4,6): 48
  (3,5,7): 96

(3,2,2,1,1):
  (3,4,6): 96
  (3,5,7): 212
  (3,5,8): 12
  (3,6,8): 36

(2,2,2,2,1):
  (3,4,6): 72
  (3,5,7): 188
  (3,5,8): 36
  (3,6,8): 18
  (4,6,8): 10
```

For every generalized-weight-admissible state, the exact external
relation-rank increment is:

```text
(3,3,1,1,1): {0:108, 1:36}
(3,2,2,1,1): {0:266, 1:90}
(2,2,2,2,1): {0:219, 1:105}
```

Thus every one of the 824 generalized-weight-admissible states has external
increment at most one, while a genuine survivor requires increment six.
Therefore no `m=5` state exists.

## Exactness

The K8 quotient coordinates and generalized weights were computed with exact
integer/rational arithmetic. Small support/root ranks used modulus 101 only
where the relevant determinant bound is below 101. Final relation ranks used
the Mersenne prime `2^127-1`; Lucas-Lehmer passed. The maximum squared integer
relation-row norm encountered was 50, and the run checked

```text
(2^127-1)^2 > 50^15.
```

Hadamard's inequality therefore certifies the modular relation ranks over
`Q`.

The independently executed verifier completed with `PASS`. Its SHA-256 was

`7539c63e736e363374e11d5651bae196d3d6187fa9089a4a417cea627bdfbdbd`.

The verifier source could not be persisted through the repository connector in
this run because code-content writes were blocked by the connector safety
layer. The finite result above is therefore an executed exact audit, but not yet
a committed executable certificate.

## Consequence

The corrected m=5 closure is independently confirmed. Together with separate
m=3, m=4, and m=6 closures on worker branches, the support-cardinality frontier
for the p=4 branch is exhausted. A full p=4 promotion still requires carrying
the four slice certificates and their reduction chain onto one current-main
branch and auditing the combined hypotheses.
